{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549306-following-someone-through-correspondence","id":1549306,"title":"Following someone through Correspondence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-03-14T08:11:52-07:00","id":1549306,"title":"Following someone through Correspondence","content":"Hi. <br /> <br /> Lets say Im chasing an enemy who flees the scene teleporting himself somewhere else. Could I use Correspondence to sense where he went? (without having nothing different from the knowledge &quot;he was here&quot; a second ago)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-14T13:46:55-07:00","id":1549325,"title":"","content":"Broadly, yes, with Correspondence 2 unless the teleportation was of a particularly short distance.<br /> <br /> That said, succeeding is an entirely different matter. The shallower your connection to the target the harder it gets, and (esp. for enemy mages) if they can teleport, they can setup wards against your attempts to track them; leaving you with very little useful information that you couldn't have guessed from the fact that they already have such powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-14T17:51:00-07:00","id":1549328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549306-following-someone-through-correspondence#post1549306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi.<br /> <br /> Lets say Im chasing an enemy who flees the scene teleporting himself somewhere else. Could I use Correspondence to sense where he went? (without having nothing different from the knowledge &quot;he was here&quot; a second ago)</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that with no connection to the target that would require 6+ successes, considering he doesn't have any ward up","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-15T04:25:52-07:00","id":1549334,"title":"","content":"It depends how we look at it.<br /> By using the Corespondence ranges chart it would be really hard.<br /> But if we asume the teleports dont just dissapear without a trace there could be still a mark or even a closed portal. With Corr 1 we could sense it and the created connection. With Corr 4 possibly reopen it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-15T13:45:09-07:00","id":1549345,"title":"","content":"You'd only need Corr 3 if you wanted to teleport yourself to wherever the target went. It still runs afoul of the massive successes spike for trying to follow someone you may not know much about, or trying to to somewhere you've never seen/etc. before... and then potentially have anti-Correspondence warding to deal with on top of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-15T14:53:13-07:00","id":1549348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549306-following-someone-through-correspondence?p=1549345#post1549345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd only need Corr 3 if you wanted to teleport yourself to wherever the target went. It still runs afoul of the massive successes spike for trying to follow someone you may not know much about, or trying to to somewhere you've never seen/etc. before... and then potentially have anti-Correspondence warding to deal with on top of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The interpretation a gave goes around the massive success need. The tunel is already made by the character before, so you do not need to reconect it, just reopen it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-15T20:25:33-07:00","id":1549352,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that's really in-keeping with the rules. Being able to detect that Correspondence was just to teleport is certainly within Corr 1's purview, but nothing in Corr 3+ implies that you can circumvent the range chart by sensing the disruption such magic causes. At best you could consider the successes needed lower by a good roll on examining the remnants of the magic in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-16T01:46:56-07:00","id":1549354,"title":"","content":"I think the OP is making a small mistake in the way the question is asked. Rather than saying 'Could I use Correspondence' the question should be 'Could I use magic'. <br /> <br /> Asking which Sphere does what is a rules question that avoids the whole Paradigm element of the same rules, Paradigm should really come first, before Spheres.<br /> <br /> Does your Paradigm use a 'contagion' type principle? In which case, what have you got to link the target to your magic?<br /> <br /> Are you a Technocrat? If so, what scientific principle would allow you to track a teleportation?<br /> <br /> etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-16T09:24:35-07:00","id":1549361,"title":"","content":"Paradigm is important in play for sure, but how much it matters for very broad questions is minimal. As M20 points out, paradigms are ultimately subject the practicality-bias. If you have two very close paradigms, but one is more practical than the other, the more practical one will eventually out-compete among mages. That's basically how the Traditions shifting to being that much closer to each other over the centuries.<br /> <br /> Even if we take this to the extreme of comparing Correspondence and Data... it's the same broad issue (you need to figure out how to deal with that big success hit you're going to take) even if the methods that are available are different.<br /> <br /> We're not making a mistake in the way we're talking about it. We're just not bothering to type, &quot;within the character's Focus,&quot; every other sentence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-16T09:34:29-07:00","id":1549365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549306-following-someone-through-correspondence?p=1549352#post1549352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that's really in-keeping with the rules. Being able to detect that Correspondence was just to teleport is certainly within Corr 1's purview, but nothing in Corr 3+ implies that you can circumvent the range chart by sensing the disruption such magic causes. At best you could consider the successes needed lower by a good roll on examining the remnants of the magic in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at it like this. Teleportation is a tunnel from point a to point b. We are not trying to find the one that teleported. We are trying to find out where that closed tunel leads. I think that cound be interpreted as a part of a whole (so the minimal corespondence range cost like fragments of the same stone).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-16T10:05:05-07:00","id":1549368,"title":"","content":"Except the rules don't treat teleportation as creating a tunnel. The rules treat it as teleporting.<br /> <br /> Also, the OP hasn't asked what you're saying, that's what you're making the case for, so I don't know who this &quot;we&quot; is as nobody else posting is making the point you're making.<br /> <br /> And in the end? You're actually making it worse mechanically. If your PC saw someone teleport away, they had a chance to gather information on them. If you're trying to teleport/gate to somewhere where you have no idea where it is save for, &quot;that place that person just went,&quot; you are literally operating on the least possible information regarding the successes you need chart; it applies to targeting places too.<br /> <br /> To pull an example from entertainment: there's a Star Trek: TNG episode that touches on this point. A politically weak planet discovers a stable wormhole in their area of space and has reached out to the various major powers in the setting to see who will over the best deal to handle travel using the wormhole and the infrastructure building necessary to handle the huge influx of ships that will want to use it. The Enterprise, a long with representatives from other groups, are simultaneously trying to out negotiate each other, while also ensuring it's even a good deal to get into.<br /> <br /> Spoiler, it's not a good deal. The end of the wormhole they're on is stable, but the other end isn't. They figure out how to determine when the other end will shift places again (good example of science at play, if the wormhole appears stable, you have to explain why in your proof that it isn't fully stable but predictably unstable), but can't predict where it will lead to next, making it too risky to consider a safe form of travel.<br /> <br /> Treating things as a tunnel doesn't mean you can make your life easier by going into the tunnel without doing your due diligence about what's on the other side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-16T10:15:54-07:00","id":1549370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549306-following-someone-through-correspondence?p=1549368#post1549368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the rules don't treat teleportation as creating a tunnel. The rules treat it as teleporting.<br /> <br /> Also, the OP hasn't asked what you're saying, that's what you're making the case for, so I don't know who this &quot;we&quot; is as nobody else posting is making the point you're making.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Treating things as a tunnel doesn't mean you can make your life easier by going into the tunnel without doing your due diligence about what's on the other side.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im directly answering the OP problem. In the variant i proposed we treat it like a tunel so yes we can sense where he went. That is literaly the question.<br /> And sure the rules do not say it works this way. They also do not say it does not work this way. I think that is a neat idea that can be used without problems. I have the feeling you are being needleslly antagonistic here.<br /> <br /> Also Portal that goes who knows where a problem? Have you played any and i do mean any RPGs? 9/10 player groups would jup that loterry machine without a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-16T11:42:24-07:00","id":1549372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549306-following-someone-through-correspondence?p=1549370#post1549370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im directly answering the OP problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you're not because:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the variant i proposed we treat it like a tunel so yes we can sense where he went. That is literaly the question. </div> </div> </div>Was already answered by Revan and myself that you can <i>try</i> but the roll is hard.<br /> <br /> As well:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They also do not say it does not work this way. </div> </div> </div>Yes, they do. You need to use the range chart because you're casting beyond sensory range. There's no exception for, &quot;calling it a tunnel.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that is a neat idea that can be used without problems. </div> </div> </div>You... don't see any problems coming from letting players skip the need multiple extra successes if they describe their effect as sensing a tunnel instead of something else? Some players will need 7 successes and others just 2 because of a word choice? Paradigm and style don't change how many base successes an effect takes. They can adjust what actions you do to make the roll easier if you don't think you can pull it off with your current abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-16T14:19:35-07:00","id":1549375,"title":"","content":"From my point of view its a ruling. Nowere does it say that following someone is a standard situation. Correspondence is connections. If you teleport those points are already connected by the other mage while teleporting. I personally as a ST feel its way easyer to reopen a recently used pathway than searching from scratch.<br /> <br /> That gave me another idea. there is a chance the person left some hair or skin sample in the area. If found that would give a body sample lvl connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 03-16-2025, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-16T14:41:16-07:00","id":1549377,"title":"","content":"Listen, I'm not asking you to like it. I'm not asking you to run things a specific way. I'm just asking you to acknowledge what the actual rules as written are so people that ask questions about the rules can get as clear of an answer as the community can provide:<br /> <br /> &quot;Because this Sphere deals with space and relationships, its Effects use a special Correspondence Sphere Ranges chart, found on <span style=\"color:#4A1A71\">(p. 504)</span>. Most Effects require touch or close contact, but Correspondence lets the mage reach across distances and affect hidden or faraway targets. <u>When adding Correspondence to an Effect, use that Correspondence Sphere Ranges chart to find the connection and then exploit it.</u> Tenuous connections require several successes, but spanning close connections is easy for a mage who understands this Art.&quot;<br /> <br /> Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> It's not a &quot;ruling.&quot; It's the rules. It doesn't need to say &quot;standard&quot; when the rules already say it applies to all situations the topic we're talking about covers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-16T20:09:05-07:00","id":1549381,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#c0392b\">Please refrain from personal attacks and keep the discussion civil. </span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-17T05:22:34-07:00","id":1549383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549306-following-someone-through-correspondence?p=1549368#post1549368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the rules don't treat teleportation as creating a tunnel. The rules treat it as teleporting.<br /> <br /> Also, the OP hasn't asked what you're saying, that's what you're making the case for, so I don't know who this &quot;we&quot; is as nobody else posting is making the point you're making.<br /> <br /> And in the end? You're actually making it worse mechanically. If your PC saw someone teleport away, they had a chance to gather information on them. If you're trying to teleport/gate to somewhere where you have no idea where it is save for, &quot;that place that person just went,&quot; you are literally operating on the least possible information regarding the successes you need chart; it applies to targeting places too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly that. Often people try to create rules and characteristics on magick that just aren't true. One can teleport without creating a &quot;tunnel&quot;.<br /> <br /> The only way I could see other mage getting *some* info about the teleporting is through Resonance. I'd say the teleport spell would leave behind some Resonance, but I don't think that's info about the mage teleporting, so I don't think even that would help in the Correspondence Table\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-17T07:34:46-07:00","id":1549385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549306-following-someone-through-correspondence?p=1549381#post1549381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"color:#c0392b\">Please refrain from personal attacks and keep the discussion civil. </span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>I have a question, to avoid making the same mistake, what was the personal attack there? I dont see anyone attacking anyone else personally.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-17T07:36:59-07:00","id":1549386,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28439\" data-vbnamecard=\"28439\">quelsec</a> I dont understand the issues there. The rules are very specific in the scenarios you mention, and as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> posted, the particular situation described is already part of the rules as written.<br /> <br /> You are of course free to use houserules for any and all aspects of the game, but at that point we are not using the forums as intented to help answer rules based questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-17-2025, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-17T09:11:54-07:00","id":1549390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549306-following-someone-through-correspondence?p=1549385#post1549385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a question, to avoid making the same mistake, what was the personal attack there? I dont see anyone attacking anyone else personally.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#c0392b\">I was asked to intervene by a participant who felt things were headed in that direction. I didn't call anyone specific out simply posting a reminder. </span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-17T13:20:19-07:00","id":1549399,"title":"","content":"Reading the back and forth of all this leaves me with a question. In M20 Core, the section on Correspondence Effects by Sphere level discusses the way that using the Sphere &quot;leaves minor ripples in space&quot; that can be detected using Correspondence senses.<br /> <br /> Up to now, I had understood this to mean that traces of the Effect would remain even after it had ended, similar to Resonance. And while they chose to word it somewhat differently, I had interpreted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28439\" data-vbnamecard=\"28439\">quelsec</a> to be talking about this sort of thing rather than a literal &quot;tunnel,&quot; the idea of lingering spatial distortions left behind after the teleportation Effect had ended. If the other person had just teleported right in front of you, then the distortion itself would be in Line of Sight, meaning only one or two successes required on the Correspondence Range chart, and you could examine the distortion with Correspondence senses to find the destination of the teleportation Effect.<br /> <br /> But I'm now wondering if the belief that Correspondence Effects leave such distortions after they have ended? Is it the case that the &quot;ripples in space&quot; only last as long as the Correspondence Effect in question?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-17T14:37:35-07:00","id":1549400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549306-following-someone-through-correspondence?p=1549383#post1549383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only way I could see other mage getting *some* info about the teleporting is through Resonance. I'd say the teleport spell would leave behind some Resonance, but I don't think that's info about the mage teleporting, so I don't think even that would help in the Correspondence Table\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>This is when things get extremely contextual. Is that the Resonance of a fellow apprentice from your youth that washed out and became an Orphan that everyone last track of, or a Resonance you've never felt before?<br /> <br /> A Technocratic security team that chased off an intruder who left behind a strand of hair in a hypersterile research facility has a lot more to go off of than finding a hair in an alleyway that sees hundreds of people walk through it and who knows how many animals that could have lost some hair in there.<br /> <br /> If there was a fight, and you find blood where the teleporter fled, do you have a way to confirm it was their blood? Or could it have been the blood of one of your friends that took a nasty punch to the lip?<br /> <br /> You can learn a lot, or nothing, depending on what you knew beforehand, and how big of a puzzle piece the target left behind. How much time you spend trying to figure that all out is also time the teleporting enemy could be getting &quot;farther&quot; away as well<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549306-following-someone-through-correspondence?p=1549399#post1549399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I'm now wondering if the belief that Correspondence Effects leave such distortions after they have ended? Is it the case that the &quot;ripples in space&quot; only last as long as the Correspondence Effect in question?</div> </div> </div> </div>The least complicated way to resolve this is that the ripples aren't the effect itself. If I use Forces to start a fire, and it leaves soot or smoke behind after it's finished burning, those aren't part of the effect you can scan with Prime the same way you could the magical flame if it was still burning.<br /> <br /> This is also how Time &quot;ripples&quot; are treated. Lots of Time magic being used on a specific place and time distorts things, but it actually makes magic harder because the distortions are their own phenomenon that you now need to deal with to try to see what happened in a given area yourself.<br /> <br /> So these sorts of disruptions and so on are more side-effects of magic, not magic itself. &quot;Space here was warped recently,&quot; is sensing this mystic static as its own thing, not something that adds extra time to examine spells beyond the normal rules for doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-21T17:00:52-07:00","id":1549492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549306-following-someone-through-correspondence?p=1549399#post1549399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading the back and forth of all this leaves me with a question. In M20 Core, the section on Correspondence Effects by Sphere level discusses the way that using the Sphere &quot;leaves minor ripples in space&quot; that can be detected using Correspondence senses.<br /> <br /> Up to now, I had understood this to mean that traces of the Effect would remain even after it had ended, similar to Resonance. And while they chose to word it somewhat differently, I had interpreted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28439\" data-vbnamecard=\"28439\">quelsec</a> to be talking about this sort of thing rather than a literal &quot;tunnel,&quot; the idea of lingering spatial distortions left behind after the teleportation Effect had ended. If the other person had just teleported right in front of you, then the distortion itself would be in Line of Sight, meaning only one or two successes required on the Correspondence Range chart, and you could examine the distortion with Correspondence senses to find the destination of the teleportation Effect.<br /> <br /> But I'm now wondering if the belief that Correspondence Effects leave such distortions after they have ended? Is it the case that the &quot;ripples in space&quot; only last as long as the Correspondence Effect in question?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically i was refering to an idea. If teleportation moves from point A to point B then it could possibly be traced instead of tracing the mage that teleported. Works well enough as a explanation for my games and is a popular teleportation trope in fiction.<br /> <br /> Edit: Now i wonder if Corr + Entropy would allow to create a &quot;random portal&quot; exactly to the place we are looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 03-21-2025, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-22T17:05:06-07:00","id":1549503,"title":"","content":"So... there is precedent in Mage for comboing Correspondence and Entropy, but it generally results in two things:<br /> <br /> 1) Adding a ton of successes to the Entropy effect because there's nearly infinite &quot;places&quot; to create a portal to, and thus you could make it a million times more likely that you teleport to the right place and the odds are still below 0.01% that you're right on your guess... and blind jumping with Correspondence still costs 6 successes. The Entropy is basically acting to shield you from the biggest dangers of blind jumping rather than being a more effective way to chase someone with teleportation powers.<br /> <br /> 2) Allowing you to swap raw mechanically costs for story/opportunity costs. Revised had a fairly fun Entropy 2/Correspondence 1 effect that basically worked like a compass that points you to the subject you want to get to. While it can't override Wards and the like, but it really doesn't take a lot to pull off because you're the target of the effect not the person you're chasing. The problem is that it only worked for physically moving towards the goal, and has no sense of things like safety, speed, or stealth. It's just a straight line towards a goal that could be 10 minutes away or months away depending on how you're traveling. So you're basically trading less successes for a lot of (potentially literal) footwork. As a ST, I love it because it's a lot more interesting to have perfect directional tracking but massive imperfect knowledge of what the trip entails so the trip gets to be fun to actually run in the game instead of just teleporting to the place you want to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}